# settings.ine — a settings-style panel written with ONLY the current
# dictionary vocabulary (page, header, logo, container, card-group, card,
# section, button, footer, title/text).
#
# Evidence-collection experiment (PLAN mission 55): feed the BLOCKED CSS/
# styling missions (56-58) and the typed-value gates with real-program data.
# A real settings panel has labeled groups, status rows, and an action row;
# this program shows what that intent reduces to under the declared schema.
# Every line the vocabulary could not guide is flagged with `vocab gap:`
# and listed in .agent/NOTES.md ("## Mission 55").

make page
page title "Settings"

make header
header inside page
make logo
logo text "Ine"
logo inside header

# A settings panel is labeled groups of rows. The dictionary's only grouping
# inside a container is a card-group of cards, so every group becomes a
# card-group and every setting row one card (title + a single text string).
make options container
options inside page

make security card-group
security inside options
make notify card-group
notify inside options
make 4 card
group profile_rows = card-1 card-2
profile_rows inside security
group notify_rows = card-3 card-4
notify_rows inside notify
card-1 title "Password"
card-1 text "Last changed 3 weeks ago"
card-2 title "Two-factor authentication"
card-2 text "Enabled"
# vocab gap: each setting row is one undifferentiated title + text — no
# status shape (on/off), no boolean value, no toggle, no control kind to
# change anything.

card-3 title "Email notifications"
card-3 text "Digest weekly"
card-4 title "Product updates"
card-4 text "Off"
# vocab gap: no state value — "Off" is display text, not an enabled/disabled
# flag; no color/emphasis can mark a risky setting.

# The action row: buttons belong inside sections and sections belong inside
# the page, so the save row is a section-level strip, not a row inside a
# group.
make actions section
actions title "Actions"
actions inside page
make save button
save text "Save changes"
save inside actions
# vocab gap: no disabled state for the save button, no confirmation, no link
# to a "reset" view.

make status section
status title "Status"
status text "Connected — settings synced."
status inside page
# vocab gap: the status line is plain text; no indicator, no color, no
# machine-readable state value.

make footer
footer text "Ine — settings experiment"
footer inside page

say page title